 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? Sure. Complementary colors are those that are opposite each other on the color wheel. For example, blue and yellow are complementary colors because they are directly across from each other. It matters because complementary colors make each other stand out more. If you use yellow against a blue background, the yellow will look vibrant and bright. Yes, exactly. Black is good for shadows, but if you want pop of color, try using a complementary color. That's a good idea. In most cases, you can get away without it. If you do use black, make sure it a deep, rich shade. Light black can look cheap.",
